{"_id":"6a2ff5432204ffbc59e5a606","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"VEetEvKGNzAO9QdZY2g86","description":"# JSON\n\nJSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a text format for structured data commonly returned by APIs. `pd.read_json()` converts JSON into a DataFrame, though nested structures often require normalization with `pd.json_normalize()`. JSON is flexible but can be irregular in structure, requiring careful handling of missing fields.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.read_json","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.read_json.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb74"},{"type":"article","title":"Pandas Read JSON","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/pandas/pandas_json.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb75"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:51:15.023Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/VEetEvKGNzAO9QdZY2g86.md"}